div.p:
In sect. 8 Cicero shows that Archias was a citizen of Heraclia and so came under the first requirement of the law; in sect. 9 he claims that his client had also complied with the other two requirements (domicilium
and professio
).

p.seg:
,
							etc.: alluding to the myths of Orpheus and Arion (see Ovid, Met. 10.3;
							Fasti, 2. 83-118; Virg., Ecl. 8.56).
